I agree.  A possibility would be to ignore bones files in competition mode
only.

>More than that, the idea is unworkable anyway; how do you compare your
>game where you race for the wizard to win the game with my game where
>I've sat on level 4 for 100,000 moves accumulating every artifact and
>blessing available from the gods to a neutral player, even if we _did_
>happen to start with the same random number seed?

I don't see this as a problem.  Given the same dungeon contents and the
same initial inventory and stats, I think it would be perfectly fair
to compare the two games.  You could go by points, or whatever.

I look at it the same way I would look at beating a chess computer.  If I
beat the chess computer in 50 moves and you do it in 30, you played better,
even though the games in between were totally different.  We had the same
chance from the beginning, and the competition is in who can make the most
of the situation.

